# /etc/default/creature-server
#
# Read by the systemd units via `EnvironmentFile=-`. The leading dash means the
# service still starts if this file is absent, so a box boots fine before it
# exists.
#
# This file is a dpkg conffile: package upgrades preserve your edits and dpkg
# prompts before replacing it. It ships mode 0600 for the reason below.
#
# THIS FILE HOLDS SECRETS, and that is the whole point of it. Unit files are
# world-readable under /usr/lib/systemd/system, so an API key in ExecStart is
# readable by every user on the box; this file is not.
#
# Everything that is NOT a secret belongs in /etc/creature/server.json
# (issue #237), which is also version-controlled in the creature-server repo.

# ElevenLabs. Only needed to GENERATE new dialog audio — stage re-renders,
# playback and streaming all work without it (issue #146). Leaving it unset on a
# travel rig is a reasonable choice: it makes an accidental dialog render fail
# loudly instead of quietly spending money.
#VOICE_API_KEY=

# Honeycomb. Unset means traces are simply not exported; the server logs a
# connection error per batch and carries on. Survivable, but it makes a
# production problem much harder to see.
#HONEYCOMB_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Travel rig only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# creature-server-travel.service bakes its settings into the unit as flags and
# reads these two to override them. The mainstage unit does not use them — it
# takes its settings from /etc/creature/server.json instead.
#CREATURE_MONGO_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1/?serverSelectionTimeoutMS=2000
#CREATURE_SOUNDS=/srv/sounds

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anything else to append to the command line
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Appended by both units. Flags beat both the environment and the config file,
# so this is the place for a one-off experiment, e.g.:
#   --audio-cache-dir /var/cache/creature-server   (keep the cache off the NAS)
#   --network-device eth0
#   --use-gpio                                     (Pi GPIO, off by default)
#   --animation-delay-ms 120                       (audio sync compensation)
#CREATURE_SERVER_EXTRA_ARGS=
